<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Guelph Hydrants &mdash; OSM Coverage Gaps</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="../index.css">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="gaps.css">
<link rel="stylesheet"
      href="https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.css"
      integrity="sha256-p4NxAoJBhIIN+hmNHrzRCf9tD/miZyoHS5obTRR9BMY="
      crossorigin="">
<script defer src="https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.js"
        integrity="sha256-20nQCchB9co0qIjJZRGuk2/Z9VM+kNiyxNV1lvTlZBo="
        crossorigin=""></script>
<script defer src="gaps.js"></script>
<script data-goatcounter="https://osm-guelph.goatcounter.com/count" async src="//gc.zgo.at/count.js"></script>
</head>
<body class="app">

<header class="bar">
  <div class="bar-head">
    <h1>Guelph Hydrants &mdash; OSM coverage gaps</h1>
    <a class="back" href="../">&larr; reference layer</a>
    <a class="back" href="history.html">gaps over time &rarr;</a>
  </div>
  <div class="counts">
    <div class="count missing"><strong>{{MISSING_COUNT}}</strong><span>missing in OSM</span></div>
    <div class="count far"><strong>{{FAR_COUNT}}</strong><span>{{NEAR_M}}&ndash;{{FAR_M}}&nbsp;m off</span></div>
    <div class="count duplicate"><strong>{{DUPLICATE_COUNT}}</strong><span>mapped twice</span></div>
    <div class="count notype"><strong>{{NOTYPE_COUNT}}</strong><span>no type</span></div>
    <div class="count nocolour"><strong>{{NOCOLOUR_COUNT}}</strong><span>no colour</span></div>
    <div class="count noposition"><strong>{{NOPOSITION_COUNT}}</strong><span>no position</span></div>
    <div class="count osm_only"><strong>{{OSM_ONLY_COUNT}}</strong><span>OSM only</span></div>
    <div class="count"><strong>{{MATCHED_COUNT}}</strong><span>matched</span></div>
    <div class="count"><strong>{{CITY_COUNT}}</strong><span>City hydrants</span></div>
    <div class="count"><strong>{{OSM_COUNT}}</strong><span>OSM hydrants</span></div>
    <div class="count meta-count">City data {{DATA_DATE}} &middot; OSM data {{OSM_DATE}} &middot; compared {{BUILD_DATE}}</div>
  </div>
  {{OSM_NOTE}}
  <p class="licence">
    <a href="{{LICENSE_URL}}">{{LICENSE_NOTICE}}</a>
    Source: <a href="{{DATASET_PAGE}}">Hydrants</a>.
  </p>
</header>

<div class="layout">
  <div id="gap-map"
       data-geojson="gaps.geojson"
       data-raster="../tiles/raster/{z}/{x}/{y}.png"></div>

  <aside class="panel">
    <div class="panel-head">
      <div class="controls">
        <label><span class="swatch missing"></span>
          <input type="checkbox" data-status="missing" checked> Missing</label>
        <label><span class="swatch far"></span>
          <input type="checkbox" data-status="far" checked> Far</label>
        <label><span class="swatch duplicate"></span>
          <input type="checkbox" data-status="duplicate" checked> Duplicate</label>
        <label><span class="swatch notype"></span>
          <input type="checkbox" data-status="notype" checked> No type</label>
        <label><span class="swatch nocolour"></span>
          <input type="checkbox" data-status="nocolour" checked> No colour</label>
        <label><span class="swatch noposition"></span>
          <input type="checkbox" data-status="noposition" checked> No position</label>
        <label><span class="swatch osm_only"></span>
          <input type="checkbox" data-status="osm_only" checked> OSM only</label>
        <input type="search" id="filter" placeholder="Filter by hydrant or location ID...">
      </div>
      <p class="hint">
        Red dots are the City's hydrants (raster layer); coloured markers flag
        the gaps. Click a row to zoom to it &mdash; where OSM has a hydrant for
        it, a dashed line joins the City point to the OSM one &mdash; then press
        <kbd>O</kbd> to open it on openstreetmap.org or <kbd>I</kbd> in the iD
        editor (each row has the same <strong>OSM&nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;iD</strong>
        link pair). Matching is by distance alone, nearest pair first &mdash;
        verify by survey or street-level imagery before editing OSM, and do not
        copy the City's IDs into <code>ref</code>.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table id="gap-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Hydrant</th><th class="col-name">Location ID</th>
              <th>Status</th><th>OSM &middot; iD</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody></tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </aside>
</div>

</body>
</html>
